# Apple client source selection - ONE repository, ONE source, TWO products.
#
# The two Apple products this fork ships are built from the SAME Swift source tree, at
# the SAME commit, with the SAME Libbox framework:
#
#   iOS / SFI     scheme SFI   -> one client source SHA
#   macOS / SFM   scheme SFM   -> the same client source SHA
#
# # What the parent repository decides, and what it does not
#
# The parent decides ONE thing: which Apple source commit this release is built from.
# It does not decide which UI a device shows. That is a runtime property of the Apple
# source itself, which routes presentation from the device idiom:
#
#   iPhone  -> the fork's Hako presentation
#   iPad    -> upstream's presentation
#   macOS   -> upstream's presentation
#
# Because that routing lives in the Apple source, the parent must NOT select a different
# commit per platform. An earlier revision of this file pinned macOS to an independent
# `dev` commit, which meant the two products were built from two different sources and the
# parent - not the Apple source - was deciding UI ownership. That model is gone.
#
# # Where the SHA comes from - the source AUTHORITY
#
# DEFAULT: the tip of APPLE_CLIENT_BRANCH on APPLE_CLIENT_REPOSITORY.
#
# The Apple client repository is developed independently of this one, so making the parent
# gitlink the authority meant every client commit needed a SECOND commit here - and a push,
# and a pull - before it could be built. That is the manual pin this change removes. The
# authority is the client repository: its tip is resolved to an exact SHA at the start of a
# build, and that SHA is frozen for the rest of that build.
#
# OVERRIDE: set APPLE_CLIENT_REF (or APPLE_CLIENT_SHA) to build an exact revision - a 40-hex
# SHA, a tag, or a branch - which is how an older build is reproduced.
#
# In BOTH cases the exact commit is materialised and recorded. "We built main" is not a
# provenance statement; "we built 40dd4879" is. A branch name is never what gets archived.
#
# # `clients/apple` after this change
#
# The submodule and its gitlink still exist and still work: the local default checkout, the
# developer convenience, and history all still read them. They are no longer the BUILD
# authority, and a published build is no longer asserted to equal the gitlink - that
# assertion is precisely what made the pin manual. Set APPLE_CLIENT_REQUIRE_GITLINK=1 to get
# the old equality check back, for a build that must match the recorded submodule.
#
# scripts/ci/apple-client-source.sh is the only reader of this file.

# The single Apple client repository. Used to resolve the default revision, for the submodule
# URL check, and for the ephemeral same-SHA working tree a platform overlay needs.
APPLE_CLIENT_REPOSITORY=https://github.com/Piggy-Cat-bit-shadow/sing-box-for-apple

# The branch whose tip is the DEFAULT source, and the branch the ancestor check proves a
# pinned commit belongs to. A moving branch cannot move a build that has already resolved:
# resolution produces an exact SHA, and the SHA is what the rest of the build consumes.
APPLE_CLIENT_BRANCH=main

# The iPhone Hako presentation's design baseline, as a tag rather than a branch.
#
# This replaces `IOS_APPLE_BRANCH=hako-ui`, which named a long-lived branch. That branch was
# retired in the repository-consolidation round: the Apple repository now carries only
# `main` (the product line) and `dev` (the upstream reference), and the historical design
# truth is preserved as a tag on the frozen commit. Keeping the old name would have left
# release metadata pointing at a branch that no longer exists - and it was already dead
# weight, because no reader ever loaded it: `platform_branch` answers with
# `APPLE_CLIENT_BRANCH` for both platforms and deliberately does not fall back to this name.
#
# The tag is not read by any script. It is recorded so a reader can find the design the
# iPhone presentation is frozen against, and so the lineage survives the branch deletion.
# Resolve the commit with:  git -C clients/apple rev-parse archive/hako-design-v1^{commit}
HAKO_DESIGN_BASELINE_TAG=archive/hako-design-v1
